Description: server: notify systemd once every worker is ready
 Each worker reports to the supervisor (main.ts) once it is ready. Once all
 started workers have reported, the supervisor runs its onAllReady hook, which
 sends READY=1 via systemd-notify when NOTIFY_SOCKET is set. Type=notify units
 thus become active only when immich actually serves, for any
 IMMICH_WORKERS_INCLUDE/EXCLUDE combination.
 .
 Ready points:
  - api and maintenance: after listening, which follows their bootstrap,
    including database and vector extension migrations.
  - microservices: after its whole bootstrap (every AppBootstrap and ConfigInit
    handler, e.g. geodata import and plugin load) and listen. A failing
    bootstrap step exits the server, and PostgreSQL may restart as soon as a
    start returned (e.g. immich-db-reqs' vchord trigger in the same apt run).
 .
 Microservices starts its job workers only after reporting ready, not in
 QueueService's AppBootstrap handler: its worker thread shares the libuv
 threadpool with job I/O, which on slow storage blocks the remaining bootstrap
 indefinitely. Queue concurrency is applied when the job workers start, as
 ConfigInit runs before they exist.
 .
 The ready report stays off the threadpool: postMessage, process.send and
 spawning systemd-notify do not use it. systemd-notify runs as a child of the
 main process, hence NotifyAccess=all in the unit.
